claimed: json-projection-alloc -- the rest of the lossless road, after
json-cst-batch-road took the pipeline out.

Operator asked what else there is. Two places, both INSIDE Json.scala
-- no shared interface, unlike the filed scan-step-allocation:

- the projection returns a Vector PER NODE AND PER LEAF to express
  "0, 1 or many": Vector(JNull), Vector(JBool(b)), and kids.flatMap
  building intermediates at every level. `pairs` then adds
  grouped(2), which is another Vector per field.
- unquote allocates a StringBuilder for EVERY string token, plus a
  stripPrefix and a stripSuffix substring, even when the string holds
  no escape -- which is nearly all of them.

Both are guarded by tests that already exist and are strong:
TestJsonValue's prefix sweep compares the fast value road against the
lossless one over every truncation of every document, which runs the
projection; TestJsonCst does the same for trees.

Honest about the value: no main-source caller uses the lossless road
(it serves Json.parse's damage fallback, the incremental story and the
tests), so this is bounded work on a cold road. It is taken because
the operator asked what remained and these two are self-contained;
scan-step-allocation stays filed, because that one costs an interface
four codecs implement.

Files: okay-codec Json.scala, specs/codecs.md, boards.
